WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.760
Jeff Goldblum returning to the "Jurassic"&nbsp;
universe! Japanese Spider-Man joining the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.920
"Spider-Verse"! Daniel Craig breaking out that&nbsp;
Kentucky-fried accent again for "Knives Out 2"!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:17.200
2022 is shaping up to be a fun year for movies.&nbsp;
Here's what we're looking forward to the most.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:23.440
After more than three decades of regularly&nbsp;
getting new live-action "Batman" films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:29.040
you'd think there's nowhere this franchise could&nbsp;
go next. But the marketing for "The Batman" makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:33.760
it look like this new Matt Reeves feature could&nbsp;
offer something new and extremely exciting.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.520
Specifically, the production's trailers have&nbsp;
emphasized a film noir aesthetic that appears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.560
to merge the maximalist visual sensibilities&nbsp;
of Tim Burton's take on the Dark Knight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:49.680
with the grimy tangibility of Christopher&nbsp;
Nolan's interpretation of the character.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.800
Meanwhile, the film's vision of the Riddler,&nbsp;
played by Paul Dano , appears more like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.320
Zodiac Killer than Jim Carrey's over-the-top&nbsp;
incarnation from "Batman Forever." That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:05.280
good not just in terms of offering up something&nbsp;
different from older "Batman" movies, it also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:11.280
teases a version of Batman that's more about his&nbsp;
detective skills than exclusively punching people.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.600
Those promising concepts are paired&nbsp;
up with the equally intriguing casting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.160
of Robert Pattinson in the titular role.&nbsp;
The "Good Time" leading man already looks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.840
like he's brewing something special&nbsp;
with his take on Bruce Wayne/Batman.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.160
"I'm vengeance."

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:32.800
Combine this cast with all the striking&nbsp;
imagery seen in the film's initial trailers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.040
and it becomes clear why, even&nbsp;
after so many other "Batman" movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:41.440
it's hard not to get excited about the&nbsp;
possibilities that lie within "The Batman."

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:48.720
The 2022 Marvel Cinematic Universe title that&nbsp;
everyone is watching with especially intense&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:54.720
interest is "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."&nbsp;
Ryan Coogler is back in the director's chair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.480
while the majority of the first&nbsp;
film's cast has also returned.

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.680
There's also new cast members like Michaela Coel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:06.320
and Dominique Thorne, with the latter&nbsp;
portraying Riri Williams/Ironheart.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:12.800
Rumors also persist that "The Forever Purge"&nbsp;
leading man Tenoch Huerta has been cast as Namor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:18.160
the Sub-Mariner, who would make his live-action&nbsp;
film debut if he appeared in "Wakanda Forever."

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.880
A sequel to a pop culture phenomenon like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.800
"Black Panther" would have always&nbsp;
garnered people's interest. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:31.200
the tragic passing of Chadwick Boseman has added&nbsp;
a new layer of uncertainty to "Wakanda Forever."

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:36.400
Typically, it's easy to see where a sequel to&nbsp;
a superhero movie is going with its storyline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:41.600
but all kinds of questions surround "Wakanda&nbsp;
Forever." What will a "Black Panther" movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.480
without Boseman look like? What story&nbsp;
does "Wakanda Forever" explore? How will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:51.840
established characters react to the sudden&nbsp;
absence of T'Challa? The shadow of Boseman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.600
lingers over "Wakanda Forever" and ensures that&nbsp;
this won't be a run of the mill superhero sequel.

00:02:58.720 --> 00:03:02.800
Considering we've gotten eight different&nbsp;
live-action "Spider-Man" movies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.480
it was only a matter of time before&nbsp;
the Oscar-winning "Spider-Man:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:10.640
Into the Spider-Verse" got a follow-up.&nbsp;
Currently without a name, it is known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:15.840
that this installment in the series will add a&nbsp;
trio of new versions of Spider-Man to the cast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:22.080
including Japanese Spider-Man and a version of&nbsp;
Jessica Drew/Spider-Woman voiced by Issa Rae.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:27.520
Producer and co-writer Christopher Miller teased&nbsp;
last year on Twitter that the sequel will explore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:32.560
even wilder visual directions than its already&nbsp;
vibrant predecessor. The endless amount of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:37.920
imagination in the first "Spider-Verse" makes&nbsp;
the prospect of a sequel extremely enticing.

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:41.040
"Nah nah nah. You guys don't&nbsp;
get it." "Don't get what?"

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:50.240
While some superhero movie sequels end up&nbsp;
just regurgitating the original movie's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:54.720
plot points again, the use of multiple&nbsp;
universes in "Spider-Verse" inherently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:58.640
means there are limitless possibilities&nbsp;
for the tales this film could explore.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:03.360
It'll also be interesting to see if this&nbsp;
sequel ends up building on the post-credits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:10.320
scene of the first "Spider-Verse," which not only&nbsp;
introduced Spider-Man 2099 (voiced by Oscar Isaac)&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.640
but outfitted him with a watch that allowed&nbsp;
him to travel between dimensions with ease.

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.560
Those dinosaurs are stomping back into movie&nbsp;
theaters next summer with "Jurassic World:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:23.920
Dominion," which will follow up&nbsp;
on the events of "Jurassic World:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:29.120
Fallen Kingdom" and take place in a world&nbsp;
where dinosaurs now roam free in America.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.640
Exact plot details are being&nbsp;
kept under lock and key,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:36.080
but it's known that the cast for&nbsp;
"Dominion" will include original&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:41.840
"Jurassic Park" leads Sam Neill, Laura Dern,&nbsp;
and Jeff Goldblum reprising their roles.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.840
The return of this trio is already&nbsp;
enough to get "Jurassic Park" fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:50.640
stoked to see "Dominion," but moviegoers&nbsp;
should also get excited about newcomer cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:56.720
members like Mamoudou Athie and who promise&nbsp;
to inject new personality into this series.

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:01.200
For those who think this franchise has&nbsp;
gone extinct, "Jurassic World: Dominion"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.200 --> 00:05:06.800
certainly has the potential to show that life,&nbsp;
or at least a jolt of creativity, finds a way.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:12.800
Can you believe it's been 25 years since the&nbsp;
original "Mission: Impossible" lit the fuse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:18.320
and blew up everyone's expectations for what&nbsp;
a movie adaptation of an old TV show could be?

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:22.320
"So hard to keep track of these things."

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.680
Rather than leaning on fan-service and&nbsp;
hollow rehashes of familiar storylines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:31.520
from its source material, the "Mission:&nbsp;
Impossible" series keeps on delivering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:36.480
fresh new stunts and exciting storylines that&nbsp;
keep moviegoers across the globe guessing.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:40.320
With all these achievements under the&nbsp;
franchise's belt, no wonder people are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:45.120
so excited to see what lies in store for&nbsp;
Ethan Hunt in "Mission: Impossible 7."

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.200
There are also lots of new cast members&nbsp;
joining this particular adventure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:54.240
Esai Morales is onboard to play the primary&nbsp;
villain, while Hayley Atwell is portraying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.240 --> 00:06:00.080
someone described on the "Light The Fuse"&nbsp;
podcast as a "destructive force of nature."

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:06.080
As if those two weren't enough, Shea Whigham, Pom&nbsp;
Klementieff and Cary Elwes, among many others, are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:11.360
also taking on new characters in this sprawling&nbsp;
series. Then, of course, there are the stunts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:15.600
which apparently include Cruise riding a dirt&nbsp;
bike off a cliff. What more could you want?

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:23.680
For years, Aquaman was a punchline, but the 2018&nbsp;
"Aquaman" movie became a surprise monster hit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:30.480
grossing $1.14 billion worldwide and securing&nbsp;
the title of highest-grossing DC Comics&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:35.120
adaptation at the worldwide box office.&nbsp;
All eyes are now on the film's sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:39.840
"Aquaman and the Lost Kingdom," to see if the&nbsp;
momentum behind this character can be maintained.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:45.680
"I'm no leader. I'm not a king. I do&nbsp;
not work or play well with others."

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:51.680
James Wan is back in the director's chair&nbsp;
for this installment and both Jason Momoa&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:56.240
and Amber Heard are returning. Yahya&nbsp;
Abdul-Mateen II is also coming back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.240 --> 00:07:01.760
a much more prominent capacity as the&nbsp;
supervillain David Kane/Black Manta.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:07.280
It's nice to know there's a capable cast involved,&nbsp;
but what people really want out of an "Aquaman"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:12.400
movie is all the staggering spectacle its&nbsp;
predecessor delivered. If Wan can deliver on that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:16.320
then Aquaman won't ever have to worry&nbsp;
about being reduced to a punchline again.

00:07:17.520 --> 00:07:23.680
"Avatar" debuted back in 2009 and did huge&nbsp;
numbers. Usually, a movie that impacts the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:29.120
global box office like that James Cameron epic&nbsp;
will receive a barrage of sequels in short order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:33.200
But Cameron has taken his time in&nbsp;
crafting follow-ups to "Avatar,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:37.760
which has resulted in countless release&nbsp;
date delays even before the COVID-19&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:41.280
pandemic threw a wrench into the&nbsp;
production of all four sequels.

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:47.840
The first of these sequels is set for a December&nbsp;
2022 release and, even after all this waiting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:53.200
the world of Pandora still seems surprisingly&nbsp;
intriguing. For one thing, Cameron is good at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:59.680
creating cinematic spectacles, period. Second,&nbsp;
projects like "Aliens" and "Terminator 2: Judgment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:04.400
Day" show that Cameron knows how to make sequels&nbsp;
that just aren't hollow rehashes of the past.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:08.480
The extensive wait between the original&nbsp;
"Avatar" and the first of its sequels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:11.120
also gives one hope that Cameron and company have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:14.880
spent that time wisely to make this&nbsp;
blockbuster as good as it can be.

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:20.400
No one knows if the world is still craving more&nbsp;
"Avatar" like it was in 2009, but the reputation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:26.720
of Cameron ensures that "Avatar 2" is one of the&nbsp;
most intriguing cinematic question marks of 2022.

00:08:27.840 --> 00:08:33.840
One good murder mystery deserves another, so&nbsp;
Benoit Blanc is back. After "Knives Out" became&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:39.040
a smash, it was only inevitable that the world&nbsp;
would be greeted with further Blanc adventures.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:44.240
Classic sleuths like Hercule Poirot got&nbsp;
called back for countless further mysteries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:49.040
so why shouldn't Blanc also solve an&nbsp;
endless series of eccentric cases?

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:52.400
"My presence will be ornamental."

00:08:53.520 --> 00:08:57.600
Daniel Craig is the only returning&nbsp;
cast member for this sequel, a welcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:02.240
indicator that this follow-up doesn't intend&nbsp;
to just play like a rerun of its predecessor.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:07.520
"Knives Out 2" has assembled a crop of brand&nbsp;
new famous faces for Blanc to contend with,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:10.960
from Dave Bautista to Kathryn Hahn to Ethan Hawke.

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:15.200
It isn't just in the cast that "Knives&nbsp;
Out 2" hopes to deliver something fresh:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:20.480
An international backdrop also promises to&nbsp;
differentiate this follow-up from its predecessor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.480 --> 00:09:24.080
as does a Netflix premiere&nbsp;
instead of a theatrical release.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.880
If you thought the "Toy Story" saga&nbsp;
came to an end with "Toy Story 4,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:32.960
think again. "Lightyear" is the newest&nbsp;
entry in this franchise and delivers to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:37.440
moviegoers the original story that&nbsp;
the Buzz Lightyear toy is based on.

00:09:37.440 --> 00:09:42.080
That's an elaborate set-up for what appears&nbsp;
to be Pixar's attempt at doing a more jovial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:47.600
sci-fi film after delivering a weightier&nbsp;
take on the genre with the 2008 feature&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:52.400
"WALL-E." It also allows the toy division&nbsp;
of Disney to sell a whole new army of Buzz&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:56.960
Lightyear toys to kids worldwide, which&nbsp;
is never a bad thing for the Mouse House.

00:09:56.960 --> 00:10:00.240
"Lightyear" doesn't sound like&nbsp;
an essential movie on paper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:04.080
but Pixar's been rolling nothing but&nbsp;
aces when it comes to the "Toy Story"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:09.840
franchise. Even after "Toy Story 3" seemed to&nbsp;
conclude the saga on a perfect note, "Toy Story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:15.280
4" managed to deliver a poignant epilogue for the&nbsp;
story of Woody the Cowboy. If it lives up to its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:20.080
potential, "Lightyear" could prove to be a worthy&nbsp;
return to the "Toy Story" universe after all.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:26.160
It's been a while since South Korean cinema legend&nbsp;
Park Chan-wook delivered a new feature film to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:32.160
movie theaters. His last film, the captivatingly&nbsp;
twisty "The Handmaiden," was one of his very best&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:36.880
works, making the wait for his next motion&nbsp;
picture all the more difficult to endure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:41.920
However, this master of unpredictable&nbsp;
cinema like "Oldboy" appears poised to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:46.160
finally return to the big screen with&nbsp;
his new feature, "Decision to Leave."

00:10:46.160 --> 00:10:49.920
The scant plot details that have been&nbsp;
revealed indicate that "Decision to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:54.880
Leave" follows a detective who gets embroiled&nbsp;
in a romance with a murder suspect. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:58.960
this is one movie where the director is&nbsp;
reason enough to keep an eye on a project.

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:05.360
It's been too long since a twisted new vision from&nbsp;
director David Cronenberg arrived in theaters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:09.440
The body horror auteur behind&nbsp;
projects ranging from "Scanners"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.880
to "A History of Violence" is&nbsp;
responsible for some of the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.880 --> 00:11:17.520
unsettling storylines and images ever&nbsp;
to exist in the medium of cinema.

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:22.880
Now it appears Cronenberg will have an opportunity&nbsp;
to add another sterling effort to his filmography&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:29.200
with the 2022 movie "Crimes of the Future." This&nbsp;
project will serve not just as Cronenberg's return&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:34.560
to filmmaking, but also to one of his earliest&nbsp;
movies. "Crimes of the Future" is a remake of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:40.160
a 1970 Cronenberg feature of the same name,&nbsp;
only his second directorial effort at the time.

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:45.520
Comments from Viggo Mortensen to GQ about&nbsp;
the project indicate that anyone expecting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.520 --> 00:11:49.200
a mere shot-for-shot remake of an&nbsp;
old feature needs to adjust their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:54.080
expectations. It sounds like Cronenberg&nbsp;
is brewing up something new and bold.

00:11:54.080 --> 00:11:57.120
Having apparently already&nbsp;
completed principal photography,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.120 --> 00:12:02.240
it's only a matter of time now before the first&nbsp;
Cronenberg movie since "Maps to the Stars" in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:08.480
2014 graces movie screens everywhere. Long live&nbsp;
the new flesh, er, the return of Cronenberg!

